@startuml
title GKE Pub/Sub WebSocket Adapter - System Architecture

skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
left to right direction

actor "Web Client" as WebClient
actor "Deployment / Kubernetes Operator" as Operator
actor "GCP Project Admin" as GCPAdmin

package "GCP Project" {
  component "Google Cloud Pub/Sub" as PubSub
  component "Configured Topic\nprojects/PROJECT_ID/topics/TOPIC_NAME" as Topic
  component "Pub/Sub Subscription\none per adapter instance" as Subscription
}

node "GKE Cluster" {
  component "Kubernetes Service\nType: LoadBalancer\nExposes TCP port 80" as LBService

  package "Kubernetes Deployment\nWebSocket Adapter" as Deployment {
    package "Adapter Pod\nreplicas 1..2" as Pod {
      package "Adapter Container" as Container {
        component "exec.sh\nentrypoint" as Exec
        component "Node.js pulltop\nprocess" as Pulltop
        component "websocketd\nlistens on :8080" as Websocketd
        component "Recent message cache\nlast 10 messages" as Cache
        artifact "SYMBOL\nenvironment variable" as SymbolEnv
      }
    }
  }

  component "ConfigMap\nitem: topic" as ConfigMap
  component "HorizontalPodAutoscaler\nmin replicas 1, max replicas 2\nCPU target 80%" as HPA
}

WebClient --> LBService : WebSocket connection
LBService --> Websocketd : TCP 80 to adapter port 8080
Websocketd --> Pulltop : streams runtime output
Pulltop --> Subscription : pulls messages
Topic --> Subscription : publishes messages
Pulltop --> Cache : stores last 10
Cache --> Websocketd : replays cached messages
ConfigMap --> SymbolEnv : injects topic value
SymbolEnv --> Exec : provides SYMBOL
Exec --> Pulltop : starts with topic parameter
HPA --> Deployment : scales replicas
Operator --> Deployment : configures and deploys
Operator --> ConfigMap : sets topic
GCPAdmin --> PubSub : enables billing, grants topic read and subscription create
PubSub --> Topic : hosts
PubSub --> Subscription : manages

note right of Deployment
  Each deployment instance binds one externally
  reachable WebSocket endpoint to one configured
  Pub/Sub topic. Multiple topics require multiple
  independently configured deployment instances.
end note

note right of Subscription
  Subscription consumption scales with running
  adapter instances (N), not connected clients (M).
end note

note bottom of WebClient
  Clients use only the WebSocket endpoint;
  no direct Pub/Sub API or SDK access is required.
end note

@enduml
